WEBVTT

00:00:00.303 --> 00:00:04.305
Lattice: a real recorded warehouse round, with evidence and reviewed recovery.

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:10.854
The operator approves three steps and one explicit missing-marker continuation policy.

00:00:11.624 --> 00:00:18.625
3D reconstruction from measured Gazebo poses, replayed at three times recorded speed.

00:00:18.767 --> 00:00:24.768
The rover inspects the bay and loading dock, then begins its return to charge.

00:00:24.768 --> 00:00:37.269
A deliberate core interruption stops motion. A fresh approval resumes the held round.

00:00:37.376 --> 00:00:42.377
The complete route covers 14.21 metres. All 271 poses can be downloaded.

00:00:42.434 --> 00:00:52.439
The bay image contains a marker. The dock image does not. Both outcomes retain their evidence.

00:00:52.568 --> 00:01:01.574
Observed stop: 0.34 seconds. Subsequent drift: 1.76 centimetres. Both camera results survived.

00:01:01.607 --> 00:01:06.109
The core owns approval and command signing. Model output cannot authorize motion.

00:01:06.133 --> 00:01:10.637
The robot verifies the signature, target, expiry and persisted sequence before executing.

00:01:10.667 --> 00:01:15.170
Local motion limits and watchdogs remain in control when the service disappears.

00:01:15.207 --> 00:01:19.709
The vision model returns image evidence and an explicitly limited confidence score.

00:01:19.713 --> 00:01:24.217
Explore the interactive tour and implementation from the portfolio. Recorded simulation; no robot connection.
